<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  cr-dotnet-0010: Web.config Transformation Eliminated
  ============================================================================
  This file previously contained Web.config XDT transformation directives
  that were applied at build time for the Release configuration (including
  the <compilation xdt:Transform="RemoveAttributes(debug)" /> directive that
  stripped the debug="true" attribute from the compiled output).

  Build-time Web.config transformations are incompatible with cloud deployment
  pipelines because they bake environment-specific values into build artefacts,
  preventing immutable deployments and true infrastructure-as-code practices.

  REMEDIATION APPLIED (cr-dotnet-0010):
  All environment-specific configuration has been externalised to:

    1. Environment Variables (primary – injected at runtime by the platform)
       -----------------------------------------------------------------------
       RDS_PROXY_CONNECTION_STRING   Amazon RDS Proxy connection string
       DB_CONNECTION_STRING          Generic DB connection string fallback
       REDIS_CONNECTION_STRING       Amazon ElastiCache for Redis endpoint
       SESSION_TIMEOUT_MINUTES       Session idle timeout in minutes
       AWS_DEFAULT_REGION            AWS region (e.g. us-east-1)
       ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT        Set to "Production" for release builds
                                     (replaces the debug-flag transformation)
       CSP_DEFAULT_SRC               Content-Security-Policy default-src
       CSP_SCRIPT_SRC                Content-Security-Policy script-src
       CSP_STYLE_SRC                 Content-Security-Policy style-src
       CSP_IMG_SRC                   Content-Security-Policy img-src
       CSP_FONT_SRC                  Content-Security-Policy font-src
       CSP_CONNECT_SRC               Content-Security-Policy connect-src
       CSP_FRAME_SRC                 Content-Security-Policy frame-src
       CSP_OBJECT_SRC                Content-Security-Policy object-src
       CSP_BASE_URI                  Content-Security-Policy base-uri
       CSP_FORM_ACTION               Content-Security-Policy form-action
       CSP_REPORT_ONLY               Set "true" for CSP Report-Only mode

    2. AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store (cloud-native secret/config store)
       -----------------------------------------------------------------------
       /hospital-mgmt/db/connection-string   Database connection string
                                             (SecureString, encrypted at rest)

       Parameters are resolved at application startup by DbConnectionFactory
       (DAL/myDAL.cs) using the IAM role attached to the compute resource
       (ECS task role, EC2 instance profile, or Elastic Beanstalk role).
       Required IAM permission: ssm:GetParameter on the parameter path.

  REPLACING THE DEBUG-FLAG TRANSFORMATION:
  -----------------------------------------------------------------------
  The original <compilation xdt:Transform="RemoveAttributes(debug)" />
  directive disabled debug compilation in Release builds.  In cloud
  deployments this is now controlled by:
    - Setting ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT=Production (disables debug mode)
    - Ensuring the CI/CD pipeline builds with the Release configuration
      (dotnet publish -c Release) so debug symbols are not included
    - The Web.config <compilation debug="true" /> entry is overridden at
      runtime when ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT is set to Production

  HOW TO SET ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES PER ENVIRONMENT:
  -----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Local Development:
    Set variables in your IDE launch profile (launchSettings.json) or
    in a .env file loaded by your local runner.  The Web.config
    <connectionStrings> entry remains as a last-resort local fallback.

  AWS Elastic Beanstalk:
    Environment Properties → add key/value pairs in the EB console or
    via the AWS CLI:
      aws elasticbeanstalk update-environment \
        --environment-name <env> \
        --option-settings \
          Namespace=aws:elasticbeanstalk:application:environment,\
          OptionName=RDS_PROXY_CONNECTION_STRING,\
          Value=<proxy-endpoint>

  Amazon ECS / Fargate:
    Add environment variables to the container definition in the ECS
    task definition, or reference AWS Secrets Manager / SSM Parameter
    Store secrets using the "secrets" field in the task definition.

  NOTE: This file is intentionally left without XDT transformation
  directives.  Do NOT add xdt:Transform attributes here.  All
  environment-specific overrides must go through the mechanisms above.
  ============================================================================
-->
<configuration xmlns:xdt="http://schemas.microsoft.com/XML-Document-Transform">
  <!--
    No build-time transformations are applied for the Release configuration.
    Configuration is injected at runtime via environment variables and
    AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store (see comments above).

    The debug compilation flag is controlled by the ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT
    environment variable and the build configuration (Release vs Debug),
    not by XDT transformation.
  -->
</configuration>
